  "summary_of_core_decisions": "The text evaluates Penelope Maddy's compromise Platonism by testing it against the parallel postulate and the Axiom of Choice. It argues that when intrinsic intuition and extrinsic indispensability conflict, the compromise Platonist faces a trilemma: siding with intuition collapses into psychologism, siding with indispensability collapses into instrumentalism, and abandoning bivalence collapses into relativism. Thus the compromise is unstable and fails to resolve traditional objections to mathematical realism.",
